{"name":"Lipstick Illusion","hex":"#d4696d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lipstick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Makeup for the lips.","A stick of this makeup."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply lipstick to; to paint with lipstick."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lipstick"},{"term":"illusion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A distortion of sensory perception where real stimuli lead to a false or misleading impression of reality.","A misapprehension; a belief in something that is in fact not true."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illusion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lipstick","blocks":[{"text":"Lipstick is a cosmetic product used to apply color and texture to lips, often made of wax and oil. Different pigments are used to produce color, and minerals such as silica may be used to provide texture. The use of lipstick dates back to early civilizations such as Sumer and the Indus Valley Civilisation, and was popularized in the Western world in the 16th century. Some lipsticks contain traces of toxic materials, such as lead and PFAS, which prompted health concerns and regulation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/330px-Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipstick","wikidata":"Q184191"},{"title":"Illusion","blocks":[{"text":"An illusion is a distortion of the senses, which can reveal how the mind normally organizes and interprets sensory stimulation. Although illusions distort the human perception of reality, they are generally shared by most people."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illusion","wikidata":"Q182593"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/500px-Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?